From dd88e3f779307ed2faddaf7eae3ba44706ecc74d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: P2ppyJack <P2ppyJack@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 20:29:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] feat(journey): provider memory nodes with session
 provenance and source-corpus endpoints
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- memory_provider: optional journey_cards / journey_session_messages ABC
  hooks (safe [] defaults — existing providers unaffected)
- learning_graph: emit provider-contributed memory cards after MEMORY.md/
  USER.md entries (append-after invariant tested), recording source +
  originating session id per card
- honcho plugin: implement both hooks; auto-paginate conclusions (first
  page was silently capping the timeline)
- web_server: GET /api/learning/provider-session/<id> (read corpus) and
  POST /api/learning/provider-session/<id>/materialize (recreate as a
  Hermes session; import skips existing ids so re-running is safe)
- learning_mutations: provider-backed nodes are read-only (edit/delete
  refused server-side)
